    "Free Neural Amp Modeler captures of a Marshall JCM800 2203 or JVM410 from tone3000.com - load one into NeuralAmpModeler to replace the Nolly amp block; Mustaine's recorded tone is Marshall-flavoured and Nolly's Rhythm channel is a 5150-style approximation.",
    "OwnHammer G12M-25 'Greenback' 4x12 IR pack - the Mustaine-era sound lives on Celestion Greenbacks in Marshall 4x12s; loading a Greenback IR into Nolly's Cab 1 'Custom IR' slot gets noticeably closer than the stock cab.",
    "Seymour Duncan SH-4 JB (or similar high-output humbucker) for the Pacifica 012's bridge - the stock humbucker is looser than the Duncans Mustaine used, and a hotter, tighter bridge pickup firms up the palm-muted chugs.",
